  "prefLabel": "Jus 401.01 Authorized agent",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Jus 401.01 “Authorized agent” means a person or entity authorized to electronically file documents with the charitable trusts unit on behalf of a charitable trust, fundraising counsel, or paid solicitor as a result of filing with the charitable trusts unit a completed form NHCT-50 “Authorization for Electronic Filing by Agent,” effective September 2022, available on www.doj.nh.gov/charitable-trusts/forms.htm.\n\nSource. #13455, eff 10-7-22; ss by #14162, eff 12-27-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/jus400.html"
}
